{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme","id":187960,"title":"Sidereal's Charms = Strong Charms: Myth or Meme","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-04T07:18:56-07:00","id":187960,"title":"Sidereal's Charms = Strong Charms: Myth or Meme","content":"<div align=\"center\"><i><img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/41504e592317c334fb3bc009ff0b88b4.jpg?t=1404480211\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> ~Concerns has been raised on Miss Anys Syn's strange behavior in the past few months~</i><br /> <hr /></div> <br /> Whether it's a Sidereal bitching thread or Sell me thread, something keep cropping up as a reason for all the illness and misfortune that your Sidereal havs to put up with. And that certain something is &quot;Sidereal charms are Strong&quot;. Since lot of the responds are wall of text so they just say &quot;Sid's Charms = Strong&quot; without any explanations on what charms are strong, strong when compare to who.<br /> <br /> Having no experience whatsoever with Sidereal in First Edition, and Second Edition stomped their charmset to the ground so I'm hoping people would educate me on what kind of effect in their charmset that help them earn that &quot;Strong&quot; word. Strong as in stronger than Solar's charms ? Strong as in pre-Errata BotBM brokeness strong ? Or Strong as it &quot;OMG it's look so Sorcery-ly spectacular guy, so it's must be super strong 'cause WEIRD! or something&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Don't worry guy, the not-so-pretty Anys is actually a doppelganger!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/aca3dee1e814ae4767544ed8b9f154b0.jpg?t=1404480203\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T07:49:00-07:00","id":187987,"title":"","content":"Well, right now I'm in a 2.5 game where the other Sid has the Medicine capstone, which is a 10m Indefinite Charm that gives him like 13B/L soak and heals one level of bashing or lethal damage every action, and that's total bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T08:10:15-07:00","id":187992,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;quadratic&quot; might be a good descriptor of their power level. Weak sid: kinda crap. Elder sid: Oh shit that is ridonkulous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T08:37:51-07:00","id":188005,"title":"","content":"If you put a Solar charm and Sidereal charm next to eachother, the Sidereal charm will usually have bigger/better numbers on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T09:15:56-07:00","id":188017,"title":"","content":"Let me see if I can come up with a few.<br /> <br /> Riding the Dragon: This transforms a person into a Lesser Elemental Dragon, and leaves them either an invalid for the rest of their short life, or permanently changes them into a Lesser Elemental Dragon. Yes, the Sidereal has to pay quite a bit for this to happen. It is still a very powerful effect. I'm not saying its a play balance issue, because the actual result doesn't seem that bad, but in character? That's some pretty serious mojo there.<br /> <br /> Avoidance Kata: Wow, I just lost that argument? You're really upset. Well, good thing I was never here to have this argument. I'm just walking in the room now. Let me sympathize with you. Or even better, let me lead you into this obvious deathtrap, which I can prove is NOT a deathtrap by gong first and showing you its safe. Oops, it was a deathtrap? Good thing I was never here.<br /> <br /> Neighbourhood Relocation Scheme: That's some pretty heavy mojo. I mean seriously heavy. I have no problem with the play balance, but that's like bringing a nuclear bomb to a sword fight.<br /> <br /> Many Missiles Bow Technique: Best healing charm in the game. One arrow heals five boxes of damage? Pretty awesome. Plus ending drought, making people fall in love, sowing fields of grain... That's a lot of stuff for one charm to do! Especially since it is scene-length. Again, I love this charm, but that's some pretty heavy magic. I mean, its bringing an orgy to a swordfight and ... winning?<br /> <br /> Efficient Secretary Technique: Who does research in libraries? Armies of grad students filing their findings so the Sidereal can have their secretary pull up facts as needed. Inventive use of this charm can do amazing things. Especially when you are trying to act like a secretive, all-knowing fate ninja. <br /> <br /> Avoiding the Truth Technique: Properly used, this is a convince anyone of anything Charm. It works so much better when you try to support your enemies than it does if you try to help yourself, of course. <br /> <br /> These are just a few of my favorite charms that I don't have issues with in terms of play balance, or play effect (so long as my PCs tell me they are buying them, so I can plan accordingly), but are just such heavy-handed effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T09:36:44-07:00","id":188037,"title":"","content":"OK, 1e Sids: Combat-wise, Sidereals were intentionally given the best parry charm in the game, and the only perfect defense that worked against <i>anything</i>, not just attacks. Blinding the Boar was absolutely fantastic...for a few rounds. They had a number of &quot;near-perfect&quot; effects on contested rolls that other Exalted had difficulty pushing through, and many of their prayer strip charms counted among the game's strongest buffs -- Charms like Earth and Sky Bargain or Five Ordeals Odyssey* were <i>ridiculously</i> amazing. Many of these effects were, honest to goodness, <i>too</i> good to give to Solars. Like other splats, 1e sids had no Excellencies, but they had one charm that gave them TN reduction for all attack abilities, and another that gave it to them for all social abilities, and TN reduction was scarier in the pre-I(A)M world. Unlike other splats, they had a lot of coercive social magic, like Force Decision, End Debate, and the entire Socialize Tree, that just worked without a roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> *2e butchered Five Ordeals Odyssey, which was one of the coolest charms in the entire First Edition. Here is how it works in 1e: when confronted with a serious threat to a sea voyage, you pay (I think) 10m, 1wp, 1hl, and the prayer strip floats there for the scene, doing nothing. If the actions you take in the scene make it so that the threat cannot plausibly prevent you from completing your voyage, the charm instantly annihilates what is left of it, and you and your entire party gain a dot of Essence for the remainder of the story, which stacks and can take you up to Ess 7 and your allies up to Ess 5. This does not require you to maintain commitment to the charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-04-2014, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T16:27:30-07:00","id":188296,"title":"","content":"Back in 1st edition the capstone charms to their charm trees were, almost without exception, nuts. And some of the smaller charm trees had Impeding the Flow or Efficient Secretary Technique or Avoidance Kata very low down the tree so you could fill up with a lot of cheap and useful effects with your 12 char. gen. charms. Playing a default starting Sidereal in a mixed game was practically cheating. Layer onto that VBoS being just as crazy as 2nd edition and you can see why Sidereals were perceived of as powerful. Then second edition introduced things like keywords and totally changed the combat system at the same time it gave Solars 3m perfect defenses.<br /> <br /> There was a weirdness component, but that was just to add a stylistic flourish to things like Easily Accepted Proposition, Five Ordeals Odyssey, or Transcendent Hatchet of Fate. That way when you slap someone down it takes them a few seconds to realize what just happened. Saturday morning cartoons might be a good source of inspiration here.<br /> <br /> SMA were just straight up powerful. Pre-errata BotBM wishes it was 1st edition SMA when you had charms like Full Moon Ways in the same style as Soul-Fire Shaper Form and could combine that with the capstone Melee charm. I think that may have been possible at character generation, but I may be mistaken, it might have required about 20-50xp first. That's not even getting into CMoS, Unnatural Many Step Stride alone ... but with the form charm active, holy shit.<br /> <br /> edit: Just forgot to add that Chosen of Serenity got to add [Essence] successes to Performance rolls. There was a charm - maybe two charms into Performance - that allowed you to use Performance when making Dodge rolls (defenses were rolled back then) and you got a reflexive Dodge at your full pool against all attacks. I think there was a Performance TN charm too, but my memory is a bit hazy.<br /> <br /> edit 2: for those who don't know this: you had to declare how many defense actions you would take in a turn. Dipping Swallow Defense and Shadow Over Water allowed you to activate a full dodge or parry (as in, at full dicepool) for the cost of the charm and thus, were actually very good. Otherwise, when it was your turn you had to say something to the effect of &quot;I take one attack at (you) and two dodges&quot;. This would count as 3 actions, so your attack would have a -3 penalty and the dodges would be -4 and -5 dice each. Fivefold Bulwark Stance and Flow Like Blood granted you full dodges at your full pool against <i>all</i> attacks. So, they were basically mandatory charms if you were a Solar because wow.....that's just nuts... if you think the 2nd edition versions are too good just imagine what they were like before. That Sidereal Performance charm combined with the Serenity Aspect power was like a free I(A)M on top of whatever else you could muster because dice pool and DV caps didn't exist (or in the case of DV, the concept itself didn't exist). Except, no one had I(A)M. That's the big thing to remember, there are no generic excellencies and there are NO generic I(A)M charms. Oh, and if someone beat you on initiative then you had the choice of going either full defense for the turn (you get to defend against each attack with a successive -1 penalty applied to each roll) or you got to eat an attack with no defense. Similarly, if you got attacked and didn't have a prepared defense you ate the attack. So, unless you wanted to get stomped by high initiative opponents* then I hope you have FFBS or FLB.<br /> <br /> DV, for all its complications, was actually an improvement to the game.<br /> <br /> *the opening charm to VBoS doubled your initiative. Yes. Doubled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":407,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","user":"Ithle","date":". 07-04-2014, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T19:01:34-07:00","id":188365,"title":"","content":"I distinctly recall Jon Chung saying 1e Sids broke the game like nothing before, and pretty much introducing the idea of paranoia combat and filter builds. So there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T21:35:04-07:00","id":188497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=188365#post188365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I distinctly recall Jon Chung saying 1e Sids broke the game like nothing before, and pretty much introducing the idea of paranoia combat and filter builds. So there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to make a third edit saying how 1st ed. Sidereals was basically what created 2nd edition Solars, but this explained it better than I ever could. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T05:16:00-07:00","id":188644,"title":"","content":"On Sidereals -&gt; 2e, it's been a while, but as I understood it, in 1e, Solars filtered attacks very reliably with stacked persistent defences then used expensive perfects when attacks popped through.<br /> <br /> So basically the same deal with using strong passive defences to make yourself statistically difficult to thwack, then pulling out a perfect when they get breached, so the game is making your opponent run out of motes. A mote drain game. As perfect are more expensive and stacked persistants were a stronger filter there was less constant (at least in theory) stunting to maintain resource economy in 1e. <br /> <br /> I think Sidereals 1e strategy used a much more expensive persistant (Blade of the Battle Maiden) combined with a cheaper perfect (Impeding the Flow) for essentially a similar effect (but worked out worse than Solars, because duh, they're less powerful). Which is more of a 2e-ish way to have that same problem (although 2e does it because the making PDV value work formally anything like stacked persistants would've been obviously both dumb and annoyed all the fans who already hated the stacked persistants game.) Plus 2e introduced all this &quot;Soak is cheaper but bad touch is bad, so best to have a 2/7 with perfect soak and another defense&quot; stuff, right? Which just added complexity without adding interesting tactics.<br /> <br /> I can't recall if 1e was as bad for high damage weapons so all this may have ante-d up less rapidly in that edition.<br /> <br /> Essentially both issues have the same problem where there is one tactic and one response, and no real element of reading your opponent and gambling on a strategy of moves, and the game is just draining resources and making sure you have more by various means that don't really interact with your opponents' choices. That's a major problem to be mastered by the new edition's design, so this state of affairs doesn't just re-emerge through negligence in testing or lack of thought in design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T05:37:35-07:00","id":188655,"title":"","content":"My 2 cents:<br /> <br /> Sid charms, even in 2.5, can be VERY powerful. Depending on how ruthlessly they're used they can be dangerous cheesy and broken - but in moderation, they can be ok. However, that depends on both the player and ST being willing to cooperate and basically limit themselves... and not everybody can agree can agree to that.<br /> <br /> That said, sid charms are also VERY limited and specific in scope. Like the capstone thrown charm, where you throw a prayer strip at a target, who then gets an insane compulsion to kill the sid, but every time the sid is hurt a magic throwing hatchet appears before the sid that when thrown auto-homes in on the target as a perfect attack - and heals the sid for every level of damage done.<br /> <br /> Comparing that to the solar thrown charms, then they have vastly more flexibility in what they can do: They get sneaky attacks, they get flurry attacks, they can conjure essence weapons, they can greatly extend range. It just seems as if a lot of sid charm-trees are missing some basic 'enhancement' charms, instead having gone straight to the cool and unique functionality charms.<br /> <br /> I mean, even DBs get a &quot;conjure thrown weapons out of essence&quot; charm - so it just seems to be like a lot of sid trees do not have that much in basic ability enhancements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T06:00:13-07:00","id":188663,"title":"","content":"Oh dear, it's seem that they went from &quot;Oh my glob, the Sidereal is killing my whole Circle!&quot; to &quot;It's cockroach-Sidereal stomping time ~ &lt;3 &quot; when the Edition changed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=188655#post188655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, sid charms are also VERY limited and specific in scope. Like the capstone thrown charm, where you throw a prayer strip at a target, who then gets an insane compulsion to kill the sid, but every time the sid is hurt a magic throwing hatchet appears before the sid that when thrown auto-homes in on the target as a perfect attack - and heals the sid for every level of damage done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect Counterattack are nice, but I'm not sure whether those hatchet with their tiny [Essence] Lethal damage dice can kill anyone :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-05-2014, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T06:16:50-07:00","id":188668,"title":"","content":"Makes a nice combo with Soul Fire Shaper Form though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T16:52:07-07:00","id":188984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=188365#post188365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I distinctly recall Jon Chung saying 1e Sids broke the game like nothing before, and pretty much introducing the idea of paranoia combat and filter builds. So there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>SMA did this a bit, because SMA were always terrible. But most people played below that power level and it didn't come up. Aside from that...well, I respect many of his insights and ideals, but Chung is one of those people who thinks that the &quot;sensible&quot; thing for Sids to do is to constantly spam Shun the Smiling Lady on everyone they dislike, so that's the angle he's approaching them from. Above all else, the #1 thing responsible for encouraging paranoia combat and filter builds in Exalted was Chung himself.<br /> <br /> There's a genre of person (not necessarily Chung here) who goes absolutely apoplectic about stuff like Avoidance Kata because it violates their sense of fairness and how conflict ought to play out. Rather than arguing directly from this stance, which is difficult and puts their feelings and preferences on display, they justify their distaste with arguments that take the most extreme and abusive interpretation of the charm they can possibly contrive, positing that not only is this interpretation obviously correct, but it will define all dealings with Sidereals everywhere in the game. This is, by and large, the kind of person who has traditionally been unhappy about Sidereals' supposed game-warping effects, and who has driven the fandom meme about unstoppable Sidereal hit squads ruining everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-05-2014, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T17:56:08-07:00","id":189015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=188663#post188663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh dear, it's seem that they went from &quot;Oh my glob, the Sidereal is killing my whole Circle!&quot; to &quot;It's cockroach-Sidereal stomping time ~ &lt;3 &quot; when the Edition changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true. A few reasons:<br /> <br /> In 1e, Sidereals had a huge number of charms that you flat-out couldn't defend against (including most of their mental / social stuff, as well as some of what we now call Shaping.) The also, as mentioned above, had early versions of the paranoia combat suite.<br /> <br /> 2e was designed with late-1e Sidereals in mind; hence, it not only had defenses against social and shaping effects, it also had a rule specifically intended to avoid people accidentally making impossible-to-defend-against social effects -- any social effect that listed no WP cost to resist defaulted to 1 WP.<br /> <br /> Then 2e Sidereals was handed off to someone who either didn't understand that 1e Sidereal mechanics didn't work in 2e, or who understood and didn't care. Large amounts of stuff was just copy-pasted over; many of their best charms were deliberately nerfed, but a huge range of other stuff (like all their social effects) became useless by accident because 2e had gone from &quot;social effects with no listed defense are insane game-breaking powers&quot; to &quot;social effects with no listed defense are a sign the author was an idiot, assume they can be resisted trivially.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-05-2014, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T02:04:34-07:00","id":189258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=188984#post188984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SMA did this a bit, because SMA were always terrible. But most people played below that power level and it didn't come up. Aside from that...well, I respect many of his insights and ideals, but Chung is one of those people who thinks that the &quot;sensible&quot; thing for Sids to do is to constantly spam Shun the Smiling Lady on everyone they dislike, so that's the angle he's approaching them from. Above all else, the #1 thing responsible for encouraging paranoia combat and filter builds in Exalted was Chung himself.<br /> <br /> There's a genre of person (not necessarily Chung here) who goes absolutely apoplectic about stuff like Avoidance Kata because it violates their sense of fairness and how conflict ought to play out. Rather than arguing directly from this stance, which is difficult and puts their feelings and preferences on display, they justify their distaste with arguments that take the most extreme and abusive interpretation of the charm they can possibly contrive, positing that not only is this interpretation obviously correct, but it will define all dealings with Sidereals everywhere in the game. This is, by and large, the kind of person who has traditionally been unhappy about Sidereals' supposed game-warping effects, and who has driven the fandom meme about unstoppable Sidereal hit squads ruining everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of weird, side-ways, group-attack, BADWRONGFUN post is this?<br /> <br /> Chung and people that share his game style preferences like to believe that there is an active living world outside the Player Characters. In their style of game it's not about the Storyteller and Players weaving a narrative together, it's the Storyteller managing the world sandbox and reacting to the actions of the Players. In that style of game if a player character is hit by Shun the Smiling Lady, then that is not a plot hook to investigate some sidereal conspiracy, that is just any of the 100 Sidereals deciding the punish the PC for something he did. Sidereal charms often ruin this style of play which is why Sidereals are often either ignored completely or hit with a nerfbat.<br /> <br /> In third edition this style of play will be explicitly unsupported however in first and second edition it was supported except for Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 07-06-2014, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T02:58:10-07:00","id":189273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=188984#post188984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Above all else, the #1 thing responsible for encouraging paranoia combat and filter builds in Exalted was Chung himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um. Chung <i>hated</i> paranoia combat and filter builds. We call it Chungian Combat because he pointed out the problems that led to it, and talked about how to adapt to it, but he didn't actually you know. Like it. It was a response of &quot;Well, do this or die randomly and horribly,&quot; not a response of &quot;Clearly this is the way a game system should run.&quot; It's a lot like blaming von Neumann for Mutually Assured Destruction - technically accurate, but missing the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T03:22:44-07:00","id":189290,"title":"","content":"Jon Chung is a &quot;simulationist&quot; true.<br /> <br /> He also seems to me to have lots of very specific assumptions about how ruthless people are willing to be in pursuit of power, how badly people want to win and achieve, how willing to use violence, the rate at which the most ruthless people tend to replace less ruthless people, etc. <br /> <br /> And this affects his idea of how certain setting points work and how characters with certain Charms would act. Little of what he says is baseless in setting or mechanics but it does get exaggerated.<br /> <br /> That's just a comment. Anyone should read his posts on rpg.net themselves, particularly the ones which mention &quot;Consequences&quot; or &quot;backsies&quot; to get their own feel for this, if they're interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T03:47:37-07:00","id":189304,"title":"","content":"To anyone who thinks Chung somehow &quot;promoted&quot; paranoia combat and not just described what was already going on: one of my players, who didn't even bother to read the rules of the game and only knew as much as I've described them to him, discovered paranoia combat about three sessions into my first Exalted campaign ever, and the whole group followed suit. What I learned from Chung years later is that 2/7 filter is better than straight up step 2 perfect spam, but that's just details.<br /> <br /> I don't quite agree with the level of simulationism Chung espouses (i.e. I don't really believe just because the system allows something to happen, it will invariably happen), but I'm inclined to believe his diagnoses when it comes to basic stuff breaking the metagame, and that's what he said 1e Sids did with Impeding the Flow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T05:15:52-07:00","id":189319,"title":"","content":"For Jon Chung's specific comments <br /> <br /> On how much 1e Sidereals is to blame for 2e:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?690333-Exalted-When-did-the-game-reach-its-peak/page3\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...its-peak/page3</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chung</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;on Sidereals: Some people think Sidereals was the pinnacle of the line, and I still think it's the best standalone subgame in 1E, but I saw in that book's mechanics the foundation of what would later turn into some of the more egregious problems in 2E, as well as a highly annoying set of assumptions as to what the GM role was required to do regarding NPC usage of their RAW capabilities.<br /> <br /> Scenelong full pool combat dice adders and dirt-cheap absolute defenses hiding behind a passive filter. High-essence geometric inceases in charm power progression making the Elminster problem look trivial. Easily accessed and consequence-free &quot;fuck you from orbit&quot; buttons that expect the GM to solve the natural NPC-on-PC usage issue of such things by shrugging and fiat. Feh.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an argument where, like I've said upthread, I think it's arguable, but questionable to what extent dirt-cheap absolute defenses exist in 2e as a result of 1e Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Instead, they might just what happens when you have the level of damage that 2e had, and the insufficiency of passive defenses 2e had, by the very nature of DV, and last but not least, the fandom's glorification of the &quot;statement&quot; that perfect defenses made.<br /> <br /> On the Sidereals Charms within their own context:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?690333-Exalted-When-did-the-game-reach-its-peak/page6\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...its-peak/page6</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chung</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent, possibly the best subgame out of the set, defining this as an all-Sidereal game, sure <br /> ...<br /> Looking purely at mechanics, the main problem was introduction of mechanics with no equivalents beyond learning said mechanics yourself (a thing the GM is supposed to heavily discourage) or inventing a custom equivalent (and/or counter-mechanic/defense) in your native sets and trying to get it designed properly and past your GM, a highly undesirable situation. This is a general trend, of which Blade of the Battle Maiden was merely an example.</div> </div> </div> </div>And also : <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chung</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically speaking, when looked at as a general MA Charm for everybody, yes, it was. This is a matter of observation, not opinion. Solar, Lunar, Abyssal or Dragon-Blooded, if you could get it, you took it, because it was just that much better than every other option.<br /> <br /> Was it balanced as a Sidereal Charm? Arguably. But it wasn't a Sidereal Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not exactly the idea that the Sidereals' low Essence Charms and strategy broke the game within their own contexts (as I understand it, they weren't either dominant to or less fun than the Solars' stacked persistant plus perfects madness).<br /> <br /> The general trend of high essence is bad, but again, I see that as inevitable given the fans attitude towards power and elder essence in the game, and Exalted the Sidereals is just a consequence of that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T05:20:16-07:00","id":189320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189304#post189304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To anyone who thinks Chung somehow &quot;promoted&quot; paranoia combat and not just described what was already going on: one of my players, who didn't even bother to read the rules of the game and only knew as much as I've described them to him, discovered paranoia combat about three sessions into my first Exalted campaign ever, and the whole group followed suit. What I learned from Chung years later is that 2/7 filter is better than straight up step 2 perfect spam, but that's just details.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely remember reading the 2e Core, and the first thing I said to my storyteller after some quick look at the damage rules was &quot;...uh, am I misunderstanding something or are characters in this game, like, <b>REALLY </b>fragile?&quot;. From there to &quot;spam defense charms at anything that looks even <i>remotely </i>dangerous because a stiff breeze can kill you if not defended against&quot; it's not a very long distance.<br /> <br /> Granted, I came from a D&amp;D background, so I already knew what to look for, but still. It's a thing that is readily apparent in the game on first read. Chung just was the dude discovering the most efficient way of negating that.<br /> <br /> Granted, he was also an ass who assumed that everyone else in the world was also an ass and not running everyone like that in Exalted broke verisimilitude and were &quot;kid gloves&quot;, and I couldn't stand him. But he didn't like or invent the problem of paranoia. There's plenty to critizice him for without accusing him of things he didn't do!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T05:32:30-07:00","id":189323,"title":"","content":"Fragile? My first Exalted PC could have taken a truck to the face and laughed it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T05:51:26-07:00","id":189327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189323#post189323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fragile? My first Exalted PC could have taken a truck to the face and laughed it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could he however, have taken a GGM? Unless I misremember, a GGM that hits with only 1 success margin will on average one-shot any unarmored character lacking ox-bodies. A character wearing Superheavy Plate (A 5 dot artifact at the time) would still get hit by 9 dice + successes which amounts to 4+ HL's per hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T06:03:26-07:00","id":189330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189320#post189320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I definitely remember reading the 2e Core, and the first thing I said to my storyteller after some quick look at the damage rules was &quot;...uh, am I misunderstanding something or are characters in this game, like, <b>REALLY </b>fragile?&quot;. From there to &quot;spam defense charms at anything that looks even <i>remotely </i>dangerous because a stiff breeze can kill you if not defended against&quot; it's not a very long distance.<br /> <br /> Granted, I came from a D&amp;D background, so I already knew what to look for, but still. It's a thing that is readily apparent in the game on first read. Chung just was the dude discovering the most efficient way of negating that.<br /> <br /> Granted, he was also an ass who assumed that everyone else in the world was also an ass and not running everyone like that in Exalted broke verisimilitude and were &quot;kid gloves&quot;, and I couldn't stand him. But he didn't like or invent the problem of paranoia. There's plenty to critizice him for without accusing him of things he didn't do!</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it was quite a shock, as at that point I was playing almost exclusively various systems of World of Darkness, generally not stressing the mechanics to the fullest and tending to take powers at face value rather than mathhammering them, but when I actually started scrutinizing this stuff, nothing ever suggested to me Chung's analysis of the metagame was wrong.<br /> <br /> Like you, I don't quite agree with his assertion that if a power can be used in some way, it will invariably be used in such a way, because that's tantamount to demanding absolute perfection and total lack of ambiguity from rules that are written by humans and interpreted by different humans, which I don't believe is possible to pull off. But the paranoia combat paradigm? He named it and demonstrated that's what will happen in most, if not all games eventually. So I'm inclined to believe his analyses of such nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T06:13:02-07:00","id":189335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189330#post189330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like you, I don't quite agree with his assertion that if a power can be used in some way, it will invariably be used in such a way, because that's tantamount to demanding absolute perfection and total lack of ambiguity from rules that are written by humans and interpreted by different humans, which I don't believe is possible to pull off. But the paranoia combat paradigm? He named it and demonstrated that's what will happen in most, if not all games eventually. So I'm inclined to believe his analyses of such nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one thing that Chung has been poor at explaining is that while the analytical position (If it can be abused, it will be abused) is hardline, it does not mean you have to remove everything that is problematic from that position. It allows you to find any potential issues and then you need to make some kind of judgement on what to do with it, sometime you might want to keep it because it's thematic or fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T06:16:28-07:00","id":189336,"title":"","content":"Yes, actually, he'd have been fine. Admittedly he was an infernal and could take enough damage to kill a mortal about five times over before he would even start feeling it, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 07-06-2014, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T06:28:16-07:00","id":189342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189323#post189323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fragile? My first Exalted PC could have taken a truck to the face and laughed it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fragile, yes. A character has 7 health levels. A standard two-hander artifact (and a lot of people used two handers on the general reasoning that it's not like you're going to use a shield unless you have an artifact one too) hits for like fifteen damage and armor did little because half of them were piercing anyway. A single hit had a <i>very </i>realistic chance of downing or crippling you, and that is before you count any offense boosters the other guy might have or threshold successes. Three hits you didn't block and you're definitely out.<br /> <br /> The only thing I'd played before that was riskier was Dark Heresy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T06:41:57-07:00","id":189346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189336#post189336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, actually, he'd have been fine. Admittedly he was an infernal and could take enough damage to kill a mortal about five times over before he would even start feeling it, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernals were designed purposely to fit perfectly into the GGM-swinging paranoia-ok paradigm that had been established by then(3 years after the core). This is why the 2.5 changes to some extent breaks them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T07:39:45-07:00","id":189386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189258#post189258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chung and people that share his game style preferences like to believe that there is an active living world outside the Player Characters. In their style of game it's not about the Storyteller and Players weaving a narrative together, it's the Storyteller managing the world sandbox and reacting to the actions of the Players. In that style of game if a player character is hit by Shun the Smiling Lady, then that is not a plot hook to investigate some sidereal conspiracy, that is just any of the 100 Sidereals deciding the punish the PC for something he did. . . In third edition this style of play will be explicitly unsupported however in first and second edition it was supported except for Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? The whole idea of &quot;you're currently in Great Forks, and as time passes things happen in Nexus that might affect your goals in Great Forks&quot; is not going to be supported? Sandbox simulation (to use the Forgite term, not the variant that seems specific to Exalted-alone to describe high levels of mechanical granularity bleeding into system-as-setting, especially with perfects and NPCs knowing the value of having them IC) play won't be supported? Am I misreading this? Buh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-06-2014, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T08:16:09-07:00","id":189440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189386#post189386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean? The whole idea of &quot;you're currently in Great Forks, and as time passes things happen in Nexus that might affect your goals in Great Forks&quot; is not going to be supported? Sandbox simulation (to use the Forgite term, not the variant that seems specific to Exalted-alone to describe high levels of mechanical granularity bleeding into system-as-setting, especially with perfects and NPCs knowing the value of having them IC) play won't be supported? Am I misreading this? Buh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without going into any specifics, third edition works on narrative logic adjudicated by the ST and the ST is advised to fiat any power use that isn't in the spirit of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T08:37:53-07:00","id":189448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189386#post189386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean? The whole idea of &quot;you're currently in Great Forks, and as time passes things happen in Nexus that might affect your goals in Great Forks&quot; is not going to be supported? Sandbox simulation (to use the Forgite term, not the variant that seems specific to Exalted-alone to describe high levels of mechanical granularity bleeding into system-as-setting, especially with perfects and NPCs knowing the value of having them IC) play won't be supported? Am I misreading this? Buh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sandbox simulation doesn't rely on mechanics anyway, so there's no real way to support or not support it by the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T08:53:04-07:00","id":189456,"title":"","content":"I guess I just dispute that in more Exalted-simulationist play, being hit with StSM is just something that &quot;happens&quot; in a vacuum, always designed from a place of punishing the player, and can never result from the narrative or kick off a plot. Which seems to be my (possibly wrong) reading of what Zirionic said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T09:41:37-07:00","id":189483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189273#post189273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um. Chung <i>hated</i> paranoia combat and filter builds. We call it Chungian Combat because he pointed out the problems that led to it, and talked about how to adapt to it, but he didn't actually you know. Like it. It was a response of &quot;Well, do this or die randomly and horribly,&quot; not a response of &quot;Clearly this is the way a game system should run.&quot; It's a lot like blaming von Neumann for Mutually Assured Destruction - technically accurate, but missing the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm aware. But his efforts had the exact opposite effect -- they made those things prominent in the minds of the many Exalted players who had been largely ignoring or working around them, they spelled out as explicitly as possible the ways to break the game as hard as it could be broken while also arguing that doing those things was a practical and intellectual necessity, and they established a library of memes and archetypes people could use to construct their opinions on the matter and gesture toward in lieu of actual discussion.<br /> <br /> They also subtly promoted Chung's favoured playstyle, which was heavily focused on simulationist optimization and abdicating decision-making to the game rules. Regardless of its individual merits, this happens to be the style that most severely exacerbates the problems Chung was railing against. Chung's perennial response to &quot;I haven't found this to be as serious an issue as you're making it out to be&quot; was &quot;that's because you're playing the game wrong.&quot; He was very much willing to make other people's play experience worse in order to get them on board with the problem of <i>his</i> bad play experience, and he was successful in that at least.<br /> <br /> The fact that you're arguing against something and want it to go away does not immunize you to the accusation that your arguments encourage that thing -- on the contrary, that's <i>very common</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189258#post189258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of weird, side-ways, group-attack, BADWRONGFUN post is this?<br /> <br /> Chung and people that share his game style preferences like to believe that there is an active living world outside the Player Characters. In their style of game it's not about the Storyteller and Players weaving a narrative together, it's the Storyteller managing the world sandbox and reacting to the actions of the Players. In that style of game if a player character is hit by Shun the Smiling Lady, then that is not a plot hook to investigate some sidereal conspiracy, that is just any of the 100 Sidereals deciding the punish the PC for something he did. Sidereal charms often ruin this style of play which is why Sidereals are often either ignored completely or hit with a nerfbat.<br /> <br /> In third edition this style of play will be explicitly unsupported however in first and second edition it was supported except for Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't the objection I'm making. See how I'm not attacking the style of play you're defending anywhere in the quoted passage? The scare-quotes on &quot;sensible&quot; are meant to imply that it's not a plausible reading of how people would behave in-setting, not that worrying about what's sensible is BADWRONGFUN. I will say this, though: you're <i>seriously</i> overestimating the extent to which the Sidereal charmset represented a philosophical break from the rest of 1e.<br /> <br /> My point is that people's arguments about how things like Shun and AK damage the internal consistency of the setting generally require an extremely questionable form of simulationism -- as a rule they tend to show player-perspective bias in how they think it's &quot;logical&quot; for people in the setting to act, they elide things that don't interest them personally even if those things are real (<i>especially</i> if they're not mechanical), and they often rely on bad-faith readings of the powers in question in order to bulk up their case. This is because, most of the time, the underlying cause is actually that powers that they can't resist causes them a &quot;bad feeling&quot; that involves their sense of fairness and is difficult to quantify, and they don't want to argue from that angle because they value objectivity and are wary of putting their feelings on the table where others can pick at them.<br /> <br /> There's a real discussion to be had about the Sidereal powerset and I have criticisms of it myself, but the tenor of the discussion generally made it impossible to usefully discuss it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-06-2014, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T10:29:13-07:00","id":189504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189483#post189483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that people's arguments about how things like Shun and AK damage the internal consistency of the setting generally require an extremely questionable form of simulationism -- as a rule they tend to show player-perspective bias in how they think it's &quot;logical&quot; for people in the setting to act, they elide things that don't interest them personally even if those things are real (<i>especially</i> if they're not mechanical), and they often rely on bad-faith readings of the powers in question in order to bulk up their case.</div> </div> </div> </div>If people in real life had the ability to infallibly ruin anyone elses love life with no potential of retaliation or even tracing the effect back to them do you really think they wouldn't habitually use it on people they dislike? It's practically consequence free since you can release the commitment whenever you want and releasing it just means the victim can start creating new intimacies, it doesn't fix any of the ones already broken.<br /> <br /> For a player character Shun isn't necessarily useful since ruining someones relationships doesn't usually accomplish any of your goals but for a real person just fucking you over is its own reward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189456#post189456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I just dispute that in more Exalted-simulationist play, being hit with StSM is just something that &quot;happens&quot; in a vacuum, always designed from a place of punishing the player, and can never result from the narrative or kick off a plot. Which seems to be my (possibly wrong) reading of what Zirionic said.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lack of narrative or plot is the definition of simulationist play. The story is an emergent property of the interactions between the players and the world. Getting hit by StSM is not something that happens out of a vacuum but because something you did made any of the Sidereals possessing the charm annoyed enough to use it on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 07-06-2014, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T10:39:37-07:00","id":189509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189504#post189504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If people in real life had the ability to infallibly ruin anyone elses love life with no potential of retaliation or even tracing the effect back to them do you really think they wouldn't habitually use it on people they dislike?</div> </div> </div> </div>In this day and age, this is perfectly doable. <br /> <br /> Most people don't, because 1) they can't be arsed to learn how to do it, 2) if they have the skills, they can't be arsed to go to the effort of actually doing it, and 3) most people aren't complete life-destroying assholes who get off on causing misery when it brings them no other benefit than this suffering itself. <br /> <br /> Also, these few committed motes don't come back the instant you release the Charm, you need to regen them the normal way. Which means Sidereals who use StSL out of sheer petty asshattery will have a tendency to die when they stumble into a bad situation where they could really use those motes. <br /> <br /> . The Sidereal &quot;orbital asshole&quot; is not a rational or plausible approach to the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T10:45:27-07:00","id":189511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189509#post189509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this day and age, this is perfectly doable.<br /> <br /> Most people don't, because 1) they can't be arsed to learn how to do it, 2) if they have the skills, they can't be arsed to go to the effort of actually doing it, and 3) most people aren't complete life-destroying assholes who get off on causing misery when it brings them no other benefit than this suffering itself while as a sideeffect making them repulsive to everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't. Anything you can do in real life is in no way comparable with destroying someones relationships with 5 seconds of effort and keeping them unable to make any new ones for as long as you feel like. For instance note how Steve Jobs, Bill Gates and Dick Cheney never got their lives ruined even though thousands of geeks would have loved to make that happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189509#post189509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, these few committed motes don't come back the instant you release the Charm, you need to regen them the normal way. Which means Sidereals who use StSL out of sheer petty asshattery will have a tendency to die when they stumble into a bad situation where they could really use those motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they don't. Sidereals have charms that make them 100% immune to that exact situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T11:21:45-07:00","id":189534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189511#post189511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You can't. Anything you can do in real life is in no way comparable with destroying someones relationships with 5 seconds of effort and keeping them unable to make any new ones for as long as you feel like. For instance note how Steve Jobs, Bill Gates and Dick Cheney never got their lives ruined even though thousands of geeks would have loved to make that happen.</div> </div> </div> </div> Step one: hijack someone's social media accounts (not that hard in most cases, since people are generally quite bad at choosing passwords, or even closing their computer when they leave to go to the bathroom at a net cafe). Step two: say awful, offensive things to everyone on their friends list. Step three: watch that person fall into shambles as they try to keep their social lives from falling apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T11:32:14-07:00","id":189538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189534#post189534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Step one: hijack someone's social media accounts (not that hard in most cases, since people are generally quite bad at choosing passwords, or even closing their computer when they leave to go to the bathroom at a net cafe). Step two: say awful, offensive things to everyone on their friends list. Step three: watch that person fall into shambles as they try to keep their social lives from falling apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>What actually happens is that a friend will call the victim and tell them their facebook account is acting wierd, after which the person will just get customer support to deal with it. I know people this has happened to and it wasn't a problem. Most people don't actually rely on their social media accounts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T11:45:42-07:00","id":189542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189538#post189538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What actually happens is that a friend will call the victim and tell them their facebook account is acting wierd, after which the person will just get customer support to deal with it. I know people this has happened to and it wasn't a problem. Most people don't actually rely on their social media accounts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Tell that to all the people who have lost their jobs, or been excluded from a job, because of a picture of them drinking, or some errant tweet or blog post that reflected poorly on them. Alternately, use the interconnected nature of social media to get them on a few watch lists- have them subscribe to the Red Pill subreddit, make them Like one of the many seccessionist parties, get them to visit the website of the Army of God and Infowars, then see how well their lives are going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T11:51:28-07:00","id":189544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189504#post189504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of narrative or plot is the definition of simulationist play. The story is an emergent property of the interactions between the players and the world. Getting hit by StSM is not something that happens out of a vacuum but because something you did made any of the Sidereals possessing the charm annoyed enough to use it on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, from reading your response I forgot (and think it's sometimes easy to forget) that the vast majority of groups don't view their game strictly through a single lens of G, N, or S. It's some mix of the three. I know I like to win at challenges, like to pursue plots that are maybe dropped in our lap by the ST as opposed to arising &quot;naturally&quot; from the ongoing world, and also have the story arise out of my interaction with the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T12:03:12-07:00","id":189547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189542#post189542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Tell that to all the people who have lost their jobs, or been excluded from a job, because of a picture of them drinking, or some errant tweet or blog post that reflected poorly on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between actually doing things which reflect poorly on you and random bullshit spouted by an account with your name on it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189542#post189542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternately, use the interconnected nature of social media to get them on a few watch lists- have them subscribe to the Red Pill subreddit, make them Like one of the many seccessionist parties, get them to visit the website of the Army of God and Infowars, then see how well their lives are going.</div> </div> </div> </div>They would do perfectly fine because believe or not, most people notice when peoples social accounts do things that make no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T12:13:18-07:00","id":189548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189504#post189504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If people in real life had the ability to infallibly ruin anyone elses love life with no potential of retaliation or even tracing the effect back to them do you really think they wouldn't habitually use it on people they dislike? It's practically consequence free since you can release the commitment whenever you want and releasing it just means the victim can start creating new intimacies, it doesn't fix any of the ones already broken.<br /> <br /> For a player character Shun isn't necessarily useful since ruining someones relationships doesn't usually accomplish any of your goals but for a real person just fucking you over is its own reward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we doing this? <i>*checks the thread topic*</i> Okay, we're doing this. 1e version, obviously, since that's what we're talking about.<br /> <br /> So Shun the Smiling Lady has two modes. It seems like we're on the same page about the fact that the committed version, while a powerful nerf for specific types of social builds, is prohibitively expensive to maintain just to fuck with people. So we're dealing with the &quot;activate and immediately release&quot; version, which costs 7m and &quot;instantly severs&quot; any &quot;romantic feelings&quot; that people of lower Essence have toward the target. It's not spelled out explicitly but the implication seems to be that this only affects feelings with sexual undertones, and that you can rebuild them through normal means.<br /> <br /> So, okay, I'm Asshole Sidereal who wants to hide out in Heaven mess with people's love lives because <i>fuck those guys</i>. I use the charm before I go to sleep, generally, because I'm going to be getting all my motes back anyway and it's expensive. I'm a representative character rather than a PC, so I'm not optimized -- at Ess 4 (pretty high for 1e), I have something like 14 Personal Essence and 40 Peripheral, less commitments. Assuming these pools are completely full except commitments, I can Shun one or two people with no big effort, and if I want to take full advantage of the full regen I'll get from sleeping, I could nail 6-7 people in exchange for putting myself at some risk and being enveloped with a burning halo of Essence that broadcasts my spending and lingers for some time after I lie down. Still, that's pretty good -- I can do this every day so long as I'm not wrung out or away on fieldwork.<br /> <br /> Now, there are a <i>lot</i> of potential targets I could hit with this, because as Asshole Sidereal, I have a lot of enemies or people I just happen to hate. Definitely the list of people I might like to peg is going to be 10x as long as the people I actually hit. If I repeatedly hit the same people, I'm going to want to choose which ones to target on the balance of how much I hate them, how much I expect the charm's effect to get in their way, and how much I can spin it as doing my job if it comes up. If I wanted to make a concentrated effort I would maintain a list and ding people on a schedule, but that's a hell of a lot of trouble to go to. Either way, for this to have a reasonable chance of hitting any given Anathema I'm going to be making something of a production of it, and since it's Simple it requires my full concentration for anywhere from 3 seconds to a minute per use. So this is on par with brushing and flossing as a nighttime ritual, except for the part where it requires spending a crapload of Essence and maybe hitting full anima. So while it's not a <i>hard</i> thing for me to do, it's a <i>nuisance</i> and isn't completely cost- and risk-free.<br /> <br /> But it's worth it given how far the effect outstrips the cost, right? Well, let's see. I go through my nighttime ritual of mashing the Fuck You button, and...what? I know in your heart of hearts that a thing happened, but it was a small, subtle thing, and the good-feeling I get would be no different if the charm were a sugar pill. Over time the initial thrill of &quot;I'm fucking people over!&quot; is going to fade, because it exists entirely in my own mind, and eventually I'm going to want some kind of feedback that all this dedicated spite is actually accomplishing something -- which is difficult to get in Heaven. Moreover, even as an Asshole Sidereal I recognize that using this charm can steer people's actions and shape Destiny, since that's what it's <i>for</i>, so I probably want to make sure I don't accidentally fuck up any important Sidereal projects, because that could have actual serious consequences for me.<br /> <br /> So, I hear that my buddy Warbert has just returned from fieldwork in Icewalker lands, and I take him out to drink that night, and while we're chatting, I probe, real subtle-like -- &quot;So you met the Bull of the North, right? Did he seem unhappy?&quot; &quot;Well,he usually seems a little surly except when he's been drinking, but he did a lot of drinking after the campaign.&quot; &quot;Ah, well -- did he seem like maybe he had blue-balls?&quot;<br /> <br /> The romance-severing effect of Shun is <i>extremely subtle</i>, enough that not only is it hard to tell if it's working when you use it yourself, it's hard to even notice anything has happened when it's used on you. It doesn't end relationships, it doesn't cause Capgras Syndrome, it doesn't remove the social context of a previous romance, it doesn't have any effect on one-night-stands or make it so the people you loved from before it was used will withhold consent to sex. It <i>does a thing</i>, but that thing is not very dramatic or noticeable, to the point where I could point to most of the Exalted PCs I've ever seen and retroactively say &quot;yeah they were totally having Shun spammed on them.&quot; To get substantial effect out of it you need to use it surgically and with specific, up-to-date information about your target's activities and relationships. The upshot is that this whole Shun-spamming ritual is mostly about generating personal amusement, and the bottom is going to fall out of that rapidly unless I can get some kind of feedback that I'm palpably harming the targets of my spite.If I begin to doubt that I'm genuinely making my targets unhappy through my policy I will feel like a huge chump.<br /> <br /> Shun feels easy and consequence-free relative to its benefits from the perspective of the target's player, but from the perspective of a Sidereal using it just to be a dick, the benefits are sufficiently trivial that the consequences and cost actually matter, and trying to get better value out of it increases your attack surface. Occasionally a Sidereal will come along who actually does this, but it's going to be pretty rare, for the same reason that most people don't block off 10 minutes a day to anonymously smear random people they dislike in blog comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T12:22:41-07:00","id":189550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189511#post189511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't. Anything you can do in real life is in no way comparable with destroying someones relationships with 5 seconds of effort and keeping them unable to make any new ones for as long as you feel like. For instance note how Steve Jobs, Bill Gates and Dick Cheney never got their lives ruined even though thousands of geeks would have loved to make that happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, see, this is what I mean. Shun the Smiling Lady definitely <i>strains</i> people's relationships, but it does not destroy them. On the contrary, established relationships are far less vulnerable to it. This is the kind of hyperbolic misreading that typifies discussions of this sort. (My favourite was when someone argued that using Shun on somebody would reliably end their marriage.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189511#post189511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they don't. Sidereals have charms that make them 100% immune to that exact situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals have charms that <i>help</i> them with that situation, but they require effort and care, which is incompatible with any policy based on spamming a charm carelessly because it requires no effort. Again, this is a bad-faith distortion of what the charms actually do in order to make your argument seem stronger than it is.<br /> <br /> Like, okay, Stern Essence Replenishment seems like the best bet, yeah? It's in the same tree as Shun, and it triggers on a successful Conviction-boosted roll (that being the right virtue for campaigns to fuck people over) or &quot;after a Socialize roll that substantially changed the local environment in your favour.&quot; Neither of these things is really something that you can just flounce into cavalierly, though -- they both involve way more care and risk than you are likely to want to put down for the kind of scenario we're talking about. I mean, if we're talking from an in-setting simulationist perspective, you have to remember that <i>spending Willpower is hard and unpleasant</i> -- channelling Conviction means that you are trying very hard to accomplish something you care a lot about. Most of the time, people will not spend Willpower even if they have lots to spare and will regain WP before they need it again, simply because spending Willpower requires an unpleasant exertion of will.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T12:26:30-07:00","id":189554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189550#post189550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The romance-severing effect of Shun is <i>extremely subtle</i>, enough that not only is it hard to tell if it's working when you use it yourself, it's hard to even notice anything has happened when it's used on you. It doesn't end relationships, it doesn't cause Capgras Syndrome, it doesn't remove the social context of a previous romance, it doesn't have any effect on one-night-stands or make it so the people you loved from before it was used will withhold consent to sex. It <i>does a thing</i>, but that thing is not very dramatic or noticeable, to the point where I could point to most of the Exalted PCs I've ever seen and retroactively say &quot;yeah they were totally having Shun spammed on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>How effective it is depends on your target, obviously Killfuck Soulshitter and The Bull cares a lot less about it then Desus or 1st age Ma-Ha-Suchi (Unrelatedly, why can't I think of any Age of Sorrows NPC that has actual relationships?). This is actually part of the problem since it's a direct justification for players to go the Killfuck Soulshitter route because it makes them less vulnerable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189550#post189550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals have charms that <i>help</i> them with that situation, but they require effort and care, which is incompatible with any policy based on spamming a charm carelessly because it requires no effort. Again, this is a bad-faith distortion of what the charms actually do in order to make your argument seem stronger than it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to Avoidance Kata. A Sidereal can never be forced to commit to a fight they don't feel prepared to fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T12:46:58-07:00","id":189559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189554#post189554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How effective it is depends on your target, obviously Killfuck Soulshitter and The Bull cares a lot less about it then Desus or 1st age Ma-Ha-Suchi (Unrelatedly, why can't I think of any Age of Sorrows NPC that has actual relationships?). This is actually part of the problem since it's a direct justification for players to go the Killfuck Soulshitter route because it makes them less vulnerable.</div> </div> </div> </div>First age Ma-Ha-Suchi is the specific case that the committed form of the charm is designed to counter, but the committed form is a serious investment, and that same type of character is the one <i>least</i> affected by the spammed uncommitted form. He's a playboy, which means both that he's amply equipped to build romantic attraction over the course of a single scene and also that he doesn't especially care if tomorrow the people he fucks are still into him.<br /> <br /> Desus was married. Romantic attraction frequently peters out in marriages <i>without</i> magic, but people stay married because of non-romantic affection, feelings of loyalty, and the desire to reconcile their current sentiments with their past actions, all of which are amply susceptible to the blandishments of social characters. If you want to use Shun to break up a marriage, it takes a lot more work -- to have a good shot at it you need to precipitate and then expose an affair, which largely removes the advantages of using the power as a &quot;fuck you&quot; button.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189554#post189554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to Avoidance Kata. A Sidereal can never be forced to commit to a fight they don't feel prepared to fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! That was my bad, sorry.<br /> <br /> This seems like a goalpost shift to me, though. Subject to its constraints, AK is an excellent way to extract yourself from a situation you don't like, but setting aside the fact that its requirements make it somewhat unreliable, the more serious issue is that it requires abdicating all control over what happens in the scene and any responsibility you might have for being there, in exchange for an unknown which is almost surely better but also outside your control or ability to plan for. It isn't just an &quot;escape all consequences&quot; button, which means that accepting the possibility you might have to use AK to deal with your use of Shun gives the lie to the notion that Shun is risk-free and casual-friendly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, your objections here seem like the sort of thing I was talking about before -- they're <i>nominally</i> arguments on the basis of balance or mechanical incentives, but to get to that point they have to stretch the interpretations of the Charms and ignore parts of their use that would matter to the Sidereal but not to their target or target's player. Which reinforces my sense that the underlying objection is that the powers circumvent &quot;proper&quot;, &quot;fair&quot; dispute resolution procedures, and the whole argument about them being game-warpingly broken and encouraging Sids to use them all the time in a cavalier way is just an attempt to justify that instinct in terms of game balance.<br /> <br /> I think there are problems with several of the charms people perennially complain about, including Shun and AK, but as long as people's complaints rely on hyperbolic misreadings and on ignoring any part of the charm's consequences and implications that doesn't contribute to the argument, I'm going to end up over here defending them. Bad criticisms erode the potential for good ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-06-2014, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:21:15-07:00","id":189601,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189559#post189559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Desus was married. Romantic attraction frequently peters out in marriages <i>without</i> magic, but people stay married because of non-romantic affection, feelings of loyalty, and the desire to reconcile their current sentiments with their past actions, all of which are amply susceptible to the blandishments of social characters. If you want to use Shun to break up a marriage, it takes a lot more work -- to have a good shot at it you need to precipitate and then expose an affair, which largely removes the advantages of using the power as a &quot;fuck you&quot; button.</div> </div> </div> </div>The relationship between Desus and Lilith is not defined by their marriage but by their twisted mutual love of eachother. If you used Shun on both of them you'd alter their dynamic entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189559#post189559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems like a goalpost shift to me, though. Subject to its constraints, AK is an excellent way to extract yourself from a situation you don't like, but setting aside the fact that its requirements make it somewhat unreliable, the more serious issue is that it requires abdicating all control over what happens in the scene and any responsibility you might have for being there, in exchange for an unknown which is almost surely better but also outside your control or ability to plan for. It isn't just an &quot;escape all consequences&quot; button, which means that accepting the possibility you might have to use AK to deal with your use of Shun gives the lie to the notion that Shun is risk-free and casual-friendly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Omicron made the claim that Sidereals with motes commited to Shun have a tendency to die when they face a bad situation where they could use the motes. I'm simply pointing out that Avoidance Kata makes that situation impossible. In any situation where the Sidereal expects trouble having motes commited to Shun is obviously foolhardly, in any situation they don't expect trouble they'd likely want to use Avoidance Kata either way since Shun is probably only the start of the ways they have their pants down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:31:42-07:00","id":189607,"title":"","content":"You know, just pointing this out because I feel it's something people overlook and we're talking about StSL, but you can use this to help people get out of bad relationships too. I mean, how is it that the first thing everyone goes to is that StSL makes you a horrible person, when it's in the panoply granted you by the Maiden of Serenity? She wants you to help people and let's face it sometimes people make bad decisions that they need to be saved from. The charm has to be subtle because if your 'friend' knew you were helping them with StSL they would likely hate you for it even though you're working in their best interest.<br /> <br /> Or you could just use it to be a dick, I guess you could do that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:34:10-07:00","id":189610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189559#post189559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there are problems with several of the charms people perennially complain about, including Shun and AK, but as long as people's complaints rely on hyperbolic misreadings and on ignoring any part of the charm's consequences and implications that doesn't contribute to the argument, I'm going to end up over here defending them. Bad criticisms erode the potential for good ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong, but so far your defence of the charm has boiled down to:<br /> A) A sidereal can only reliably dick over two people in the world which limits the number of people dicked over.<br /> B) It's only effective against people that have meaningful romantic relationships and those don't exist so nyah!<br /> <br /> I don't see that as much of a defence. If we pretend for a moment there exist a person in the world with important romantic relationships and that person for some reason is on the wrong side of Sidereal wrath. Why exactly wouldn't the Sidereal destroy those relationships and what exactly can the victim do about it? You already agree that it's 100% risk free to break the intimacies each night. I presume you also agree that it's 100% safe to keep the committed effect up when for instance you have bureau work to do in Yu-Shan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 07-06-2014, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T14:38:50-07:00","id":189650,"title":"","content":"Look, leave aside for a moment whether you think it is plausible, in general, that some significant fraction of Sidereals will go around orbital-nuking relationships entirely consequence-free. Is it good to have a statement that they <i>can</i> do this, and they just don't <i>feel</i> like it? Is that an appropriate statement to make about the breadth of Sidereal power: &quot;Yes, a Sidereal absolutely could make you unlovable <i>from another dimension</i>, with no way for you, Solar God-King, to track it back to him or prevent the effect&quot;?<br /> <br /> Because if that's a statement the game makes because it <i>is</i> supposed to happen to you sometimes, with no plausible chance of reprisal, well, that's kinda stupid, right? It doesn't even have the excuse of generating plots, because, again, <i>another dimension</i>, with <i>no way to track it back to him</i>. And so it's incentive, as others have noted, to play someone with no romantic attachments, which is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> And if it <i>isn't</i> supposed to happen to you sometimes, then the Charm doesn't really need to work that way, does it? If it's only really supposed to enable interesting mortal-manipulation strategies, it could have been written to allow some kind of meaningful defense.<br /> <br /> Either way, it's a bad Charm, and noting that it was a bad Charm was not unreasonable on Chung's part. I think it's a bit uncharitable to read his position as &quot;This will inevitably happen to your PC, specifically, or you're cheating&quot;; I've usually seen him argue something closer to &quot;Game-wrecking powers should not be contingent on an NPC not being in the mood to wreck the game with them,&quot; which again, kinda reasonable.<br /> <br /> (The response to people who haven't degenerated into paranoia combat is also much less &quot;You're playing wrong&quot; than &quot;You're playing with a very congenial set of social contracts that I would find unpleasant to play with, and/or you've been lucky enough not to hit a mine so far.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T15:00:39-07:00","id":189658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189610#post189610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but so far your defence of the charm has boiled down to:<br /> A) A sidereal can only reliably dick over two people in the world which limits the number of people dicked over.<br /> B) It's only effective against people that have meaningful romantic relationships and those don't exist so nyah!<br /> <br /> I don't see that as much of a defence. If we pretend for a moment there exist a person in the world with important romantic relationships and that person for some reason is on the wrong side of Sidereal wrath. Why exactly wouldn't the Sidereal destroy those relationships and what exactly can the victim do about it? You already agree that it's 100% risk free to break the intimacies each night. I presume you also agree that it's 100% safe to keep the committed effect up when for instance you have bureau work to do in Yu-Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because I'm not so much defending the charm as I am attacking certain lines of criticism. As I said earlier, I have a number of problems with Shun, and I think we have some degree of agreement about what those problems are. But if the point in contention is &quot;realistically, Sidereals would be using this power all the time just to fuck with people&quot; then no, that does not seem remotely realistic to me, and I'm skeptical of the notion that it contributed to 1e paranoia builds, as well.<br /> <br /> Suppose we posit the following situation: I am a Sidereal who endured the purchase of Shun the Smiling Lady and has no compunctions about using it in petty ways to hurt my enemies. I have an enemy who has important romantic relationships (or relies heavily on their looks and appeal), and I am aware of that fact. In this case, yes, I would probably use Shun once on them in a while out of spite, and I might even go for the committed version if I have reason to believe that they are entering a short window in which it could radically alter their destiny. I'm sure as hell not going to be spamming it all the time even from Heaven, but I would certainly avail myself of it<i>. </i>Is this a problem, from a game design perspective? I think it is. But it doesn't mean is that this will be a common situation even for PCs with something to lose to Shun, or that (as you repeatedly imply) Shun by itself can &quot;destroy relationships&quot; with any level of reliability. The more the arguments against the charm focus on dubious hyperbole, exaggerating its effects and the effect it would have on the setting, the less possible it is to discuss its actual problems.<br /> <br /> As I said before, bad arguments get in the way of good ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T15:08:27-07:00","id":189665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189658#post189658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because I'm not so much defending the charm as I am attacking certain lines of criticism. As I said earlier, I have a number of problems with Shun, and I think we have some degree of agreement about what those problems are. But if the point in contention is &quot;realistically, Sidereals would be using this power all the time just to fuck with people&quot; then no, that does not seem remotely realistic to me, and I'm skeptical of the notion that it contributed to 1e paranoia builds, as well.<br /> <br /> Suppose we posit the following situation: I am a Sidereal who endured the purchase of Shun the Smiling Lady and has no compunctions about using it in petty ways to hurt my enemies. I have an enemy who has important romantic relationships (or relies heavily on their looks and appeal), and I am aware of that fact. In this case, yes, I would probably use Shun once on them in a while out of spite, and I might even go for the committed version if I have reason to believe that they are entering a short window in which it could radically alter their destiny. I'm sure as hell not going to be spamming it all the time even from Heaven, but I would certainly avail myself of it<i>. </i>Is this a problem, from a game design perspective? I think it is. But it doesn't mean is that this will be a common situation even for PCs with something to lose to Shun, or that (as you repeatedly imply) Shun by itself can &quot;destroy relationships&quot; with any level of reliability. The more the arguments against the charm focus on dubious hyperbole, exaggerating its effects and the effect it would have on the setting, the less possible it is to discuss its actual problems.<br /> <br /> As I said before, bad arguments get in the way of good ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's say you are a bronze faction sidereal. You look outside your window, and see a Zenith trying to do zenith things. You are bronze faction. You want all solars to die and go to superhell. Is it worth throwing Shun on a social character, reducing his Appearance to 1 (which means at least +1 MDV to everyone), and breaking any romantic intimacies he might have (and any romantic intimacies his cultists might have towards him)? Absolutely. At the very least it would poison his life until the assassination squad arives. And the Zenith can't do anything to protect himself here. A Sidereal can break your social character with no consequences from the safety of his office. And there is nothing you can do about it. This is bad, and shouldn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T15:12:43-07:00","id":189666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189658#post189658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The more the arguments against the charm focus on dubious hyperbole, exaggerating its effects and the effect it would have on the setting, the less possible it is to discuss its actual problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the hyperbole in this thread has been written by you. Noone has ever argued that Shun is something that would be used all the time, it has been argued that if you have romantic relationships and you make an enemy of a sidereal, your relationships are going to be destroyed without you being able to do anything about it because there is absolutely no reason for the Sidereal not to do it. This is not expected to happen often but just the fact it is reasonable to happen is pretty stupid.<br /> <br /> When Jenna Moran wrote the charm she wrote it under the assumption it would only be used by PCs on NPCs or if used on a PC it would be part of a plot, she never considered the idea that an NPC could use the charm without a plot in mind. The other 1e Sidereal charm that Chung objects to is Trancendent Hatchet of Fate which works entirely through ST fiat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189658#post189658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it doesn't mean is that this will be a common situation even for PCs with something to lose to Shun, or that (as you repeatedly imply) Shun by itself can &quot;destroy relationships&quot; with any level of reliability.</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition it destroys romantic relationships, if your relationship isn't romantic it will obviously be fine however it can still suffer from the appearance penalty if the Sidereal feels like commiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 07-06-2014, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T16:36:19-07:00","id":189695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189665#post189665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's say you are a bronze faction sidereal. You look outside your window, and see a Zenith trying to do zenith things. You are bronze faction. You want all solars to die and go to superhell. Is it worth throwing Shun on a social character, reducing his Appearance to 1 (which means at least +1 MDV to everyone), and breaking any romantic intimacies he might have (and any romantic intimacies his cultists might have towards him)? Absolutely. At the very least it would poison his life until the assassination squad arives. And the Zenith can't do anything to protect himself here. A Sidereal can break your social character with no consequences from the safety of his office. And there is nothing you can do about it. This is bad, and shouldn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there is something you can do about it, kill that stupid Sidereal who decided to mess with the wrong guy. Using this on important personages can completely blow up in your face as a Sidereal, most of all because your boss happens to be the Maiden of Serenity and she might be a bit pissed off that you're using her powers casually to destroy things that are serene out of petty spite. When your job is to protect Creation, going around and finding powerful people and specifically going out of your way to ruin their empathy for those around them I think that might just be grounds for an audit based on sheer incompetence. Can you imagine the reputation you'd earn in an environment like Yu-Shan if you were known to use StSL on people with no compunction? It would be like painting an enormous target on your back. Every time some deity that you've offended (real or imagined offense) has a falling out with a partner you're the first one in the room everyone looks at.<br /> <br /> If your ST is having your characters get targeted by random Sidereals using StSL that's because your ST is a dick and the Sidereal doing that is a moron who should know better than to mess with people's personal lives. For a splat about being a disaffected secret agent that's very unusual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":407,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","user":"Ithle","date":". 07-06-2014, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T16:56:41-07:00","id":189703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189665#post189665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say you are a bronze faction sidereal. You look outside your window, and see a Zenith trying to do zenith things. You are bronze faction. You want all solars to die and go to superhell. Is it worth throwing Shun on a social character, reducing his Appearance to 1 (which means at least +1 MDV to everyone), and breaking any romantic intimacies he might have (and any romantic intimacies his cultists might have towards him)? Absolutely. At the very least it would poison his life until the assassination squad arives. And the Zenith can't do anything to protect himself here. A Sidereal can break your social character with no consequences from the safety of his office. And there is nothing you can do about it. This is bad, and shouldn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to generally fit with the realm of how Sidereals were originally conceived, though - secret masters of the world with fate powers and whatnot. <br /> <br /> My literal first game of Exalted involved a Sidereal player using Shun on the other (Solar) PC's to 'keep them on task,' so I'm a little biased, I think it's a ridiculously shitty charm and shouldn't exist anymore, but I'm guessing that the ability of Sidereals to have untraceable nuke-from-orbit fate powers is going to increase in 3e. I just hope Shun isn't kept in. <br /> <br /> Fundamentally it'd be used quite frequently by Sidereals on anyone they didn't like - setting aside petty squabbles in Yu Shan, any given Solar could expect to be hit with this by the Bronze faction, especially if you have contact with them in any way. If you defeat a Bronze Faction hit squad, just expect Shun as a matter of course. Why wouldn't they do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1165-hecaton","name":"Hecaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T17:10:46-07:00","id":189710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ithle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189695#post189695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually there is something you can do about it, kill that stupid Sidereal who decided to mess with the wrong guy. Using this on important personages can completely blow up in your face as a Sidereal, most of all because your boss happens to be the Maiden of Serenity and she might be a bit pissed off that you're using her powers casually to destroy things that are serene out of petty spite. When your job is to protect Creation, going around and finding powerful people and specifically going out of your way to ruin their empathy for those around them I think that might just be grounds for an audit based on sheer incompetence. Can you imagine the reputation you'd earn in an environment like Yu-Shan if you were known to use StSL on people with no compunction? It would be like painting an enormous target on your back. Every time some deity that you've offended (real or imagined offense) has a falling out with a partner you're the first one in the room everyone looks at.<br /> <br /> If your ST is having your characters get targeted by random Sidereals using StSL that's because your ST is a dick and the Sidereal doing that is a moron who should know better than to mess with people's personal lives. For a splat about being a disaffected secret agent that's very unusual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usurpation sure as hell didn't make the Maidens turn on Sidereals, so I'm not sure why screwing with a single Solar would. Are you arguing that this charm shouldn't be used on Solars ever? Because then I'd like &quot;doesn't work on Solars&quot; in the descripton. And Sidereals are already hated by everyone in Yu-Shan, so I can't imagine how it would get worse (or how the gods would know the mechanics of secret sidereal charms).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T17:17:49-07:00","id":189712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189665#post189665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's say you are a bronze faction sidereal. You look outside your window, and see a Zenith trying to do zenith things. You are bronze faction. You want all solars to die and go to superhell. Is it worth throwing Shun on a social character, reducing his Appearance to 1 (which means at least +1 MDV to everyone), and breaking any romantic intimacies he might have (and any romantic intimacies his cultists might have towards him)? Absolutely. At the very least it would poison his life until the assassination squad arives. And the Zenith can't do anything to protect himself here. A Sidereal can break your social character with no consequences from the safety of his office. And there is nothing you can do about it. This is bad, and shouldn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, setting aside the &quot;if you look outside your window and see a zenith trying to zenith things&quot; element, which is kind of a weird hypothetical -- there's a reason I was talking about the 1e charm. In 1e, reducing someone's Appearance to 1 did essentially nothing, because Appearance was a build trap for vain people, as in most of the oWoD games. By default it was used for seduction, I think <i>possibly</i> you could use it to make a good impression at party, otherwise it was basically just a thing you could roll in place of Charisma if you wanted. Lunars didn't even have Appearance charms in 1e, that's how much of a fake trap stat it was. 2e imported the Appearance nerf without realizing that it actually mattered in 2e and seriously fucked up the charm in the process, but in 1e it was pretty much meaningless.<br /> <br /> We can definitely agree that Shun is far more useful if you are <i>right there</i> to micromanage its application, however.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189666#post189666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the hyperbole in this thread has been written by you. Noone has ever argued that Shun is something that would be used all the time, it has been argued that if you have romantic relationships and you make an enemy of a sidereal, your relationships are going to be destroyed without you being able to do anything about it because there is absolutely no reason for the Sidereal not to do it. This is not expected to happen often but just the fact it is reasonable to happen is pretty stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going back and reviewing, I think we might have talked past one another. I was specifically aiming for the argument that Shun would be used frequently just for the hell of it on anyone who has ever pissed off a Sidereal, which hadn't previously come up in this thread but is absolutely an argument that I have seen made in the past, and you responded:<br /> <i>&quot;If people in real life had the ability to infallibly ruin anyone elses love life with no potential of retaliation or even tracing the effect back to them do you really think they wouldn't habitually use it on people they dislike?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Which I took to me you arguing that, in fact, it would be used all the time. And it still kind of looks that way to me, but I can see how you might have read my original post as meaning that from a simulationist perspective it would <i>never</i> get used that way, which wasn't my intention.<br /> <br /> But the main hyperbole I've been accusing you of here is in the vein of:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189666#post189666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By definition it destroys romantic relationships, if your relationship isn't romantic it will obviously be fine however it can still suffer from the appearance penalty if the Sidereal feels like commiting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am willing to believe at this point that maybe we just read the charm differently, but I still think my reading is closer to the intention, and if there are two possible readings it seems reasonable to go with the less broken one.<br /> <br /> Here is what Shun the Smiling Lady does, minus the committed power which is essentially a hard nerf to people who use their looks and magnetism to charm others:<br /> <i>&quot;If anyone with permanent Essence less than the Sidereal's own has romantic feelings for the target, those feelings are instantly severed. They do not return when the Charm ends.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I think it is a <i>tremendous</i> stretch to suggest that this effect &quot;destroys romantic relationships&quot;, especially if you want to extend &quot;romantic relationships&quot; to include any sort of coupling between people who might sometimes have sex. &quot;Romantic relationships&quot; is kind of a complicated term to begin with, for that matter, since relationships that begin as purely romantic nearly always become far less so over time if they survive, but it's still the same relationship, so is that a &quot;romantic relationship&quot;?<br /> <br /> If you just staple this effect to someone's relatonship as a Hail Mary, it <i>might</i> destroy that relationship in the long term, but there's every chance the relationship will keep going on inertia alone, since romance is mostly important during the early bootstrapping phase anyway. Conversely, most relationships fail <i>anyway</i>, so if you use the Charm and the relationship fails within the next six months, did it matter? It's a very good way to get your foot in the door if you're out in the field and actively meddling, particularly when using the rest of the Socialize tree, but I very much doubt that the intention of the charm was that you remove the &quot;romantic feelings&quot; linchpin and the relationship automatically flies apart.<br /> <br /> If I thought Shun was anywhere near as effective at fucking up people's domestic lives as people seem to think, I would probably feel considerably more hostility towards it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-06-2014, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T18:22:43-07:00","id":189738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189542#post189542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternately, use the interconnected nature of social media to get them on a few watch lists- have them subscribe to the Red Pill subreddit, make them Like one of the many seccessionist parties, get them to visit the website of the Army of God and Infowars, then see how well their lives are going.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of these things would be more than moderately irritating. Ruining lives is actually pretty hard.<br /> <br /> Killing people is comparatively easy, but it has consequences.<br /> <br /> Not interested in discussing Shun the Smiling Lady.<br /> <br /> Also, can we not try to deconstruct Chung's psychology? It's a little creepy, he doesn't even post here anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T18:57:33-07:00","id":189773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189710#post189710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usurpation sure as hell didn't make the Maidens turn on Sidereals, so I'm not sure why screwing with a single Solar would. Are you arguing that this charm shouldn't be used on Solars ever? Because then I'd like &quot;doesn't work on Solars&quot; in the descripton. And Sidereals are already hated by everyone in Yu-Shan, so I can't imagine how it would get worse (or how the gods would know the mechanics of secret sidereal charms).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThey'll sure as hell turn against /that/ Sidereal though, you know, that guy who keeps screwing up Fate for petty reasons and making the Fivescore Fellowship look like fools. People with that level of vindictiveness will almost certainly have a litany of enemies so I wouldn't expect to see a lot of fallout from auditing them. I guess it's a good thing the gods most likely to be aware of the charm StSL are also the Sidereal's boss and co-workers. Using the charm on Solars because 'I hate Solars' is just plain dumb, using it on /that/ Solar because I hate him or her, makes more sense. So, if you get hit by StSL there's probably a reason even if you're not aware of it. It's not just 'oh a Solar, StSL activate!'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T19:21:38-07:00","id":189781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ithle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189607#post189607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, just pointing this out because I feel it's something people overlook and we're talking about StSL, but you can use this to help people get out of bad relationships too. I mean, how is it that the first thing everyone goes to is that StSL makes you a horrible person, when it's in the panoply granted you by the Maiden of Serenity? She wants you to help people and let's face it sometimes people make bad decisions that they need to be saved from. The charm has to be subtle because if your 'friend' knew you were helping them with StSL they would likely hate you for it even though you're working in their best interest.<br /> <br /> Or you could just use it to be a dick, I guess you could do that too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because for a time, Sidereal Socialize was hailed as the most evil charmtree and the purest example of Sidereal dick-ness so it's kinda affected the perception of newbie like me about the charm, and it's all because of a stupid last sentence in the Lovers Sign's description.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Sidereals</b> generally take this constellation to explain a great deal about the outlook of the Maidens. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T19:39:27-07:00","id":189823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ithle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189773#post189773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThey'll sure as hell turn against /that/ Sidereal though, you know, that guy who keeps screwing up Fate for petty reasons and making the Fivescore Fellowship look like fools.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall any evidence suggesting the Maidens care how Sids use their Charms or police them for using their Charms, beyond the high cost of Greater Astrology. Some kind of IAB inside the Bureau of Destiny might care and/or police, though, especially if you're trying to arrange a war to end by making the rulers' kids fall in love and Earl keeps screwing it up for giggles...aside from that, if they don't have a ton more pressing matters to attend to I don't see why anyone would really care, the Exalted screw with Destiny just by existing and spending motes, after all, and there aren't enough Sids to police all the issues they stir up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T20:28:06-07:00","id":189887,"title":"","content":"As far as &quot;policing&quot; goes, the maidens basically <i>are</i> fate. Sidereals are destined to exalt from birth by the living embodiements of <b>Serenity</b>, <b>Journeys</b>, <b>Secrets</b>, <b>Endings</b> and <b>Battles</b>. Sidereals that would use their powers in ways that the Fates don't want them to basically <i>don't exist</i> because they can opt to just <i>not choose those people</i>, having foreknowledge of how things will pan out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T21:46:44-07:00","id":189921,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Maidens fare any better than the Sidereals at taking into account things outside of Fate in their fate-planning. Like, could it happen that someone is fated to Exalt as a Sidereal but is killed by something outside of Fate (or, perhaps more likely, such an event triggering Exaltation before planned/predicted)? And if so, would that send the Maidens/the bureau of Destiny into redrawing a lot of plans, or would they have contingencies in place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T22:00:58-07:00","id":189927,"title":"","content":"The Maidens of Destiny can see beyond the confines of Fate; it's a bit risky, though, because whatever they see when they invoke <i>samsara</i>, they <b>must</b> allow to come to pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T02:17:30-07:00","id":190043,"title":"","content":"&quot;Be weary when drinking tea, for hidden inside the cup may be a Sidereal prepared to punch you into a duck.&quot; - old First Edition Exalted saying.<br /> <br /> It wasn't called &quot;Paranoia Combat&quot; back then, but the concept of being utterly destroyed by a ninja Sidereal in a tea cup was a thing back in 1st edition, and that was the basis around which Paranoia Combat formed; have a perfect defense combo'd with a Surprise Negation charm and use them all the time, or a hidden Sidereal will punch you into a duck.<br /> <br /> As for Shun the Smiling Lady, it quickly falls apart in the game setting as there's no reason why the Bronze Faction Exalted wouldn't frequently use that charm on the Anathema targeted by a Wyld Hunt. When you're on a Wyld Hunt, you want to cut the target off from his allies, and Shun the Smiling Lady is a wonderful charm for cutting off his closest and dearest friends. It will also cause a fair amount of confusion and worry in the target, as the love of his life suddenly rejects him - that coupled with the knowledge that he has transformed into one of the Anathema, would be a wonderful way of mentally breaking your target. &quot;I've just turned into a monster and my wife and children all dislike me now!&quot;<br /> <br /> As PC's are frequently Anathema and would often be the targets of a Wyld Hunt, that means that they would logically be the victims of StSL. Oops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-07-2014, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T04:32:08-07:00","id":190130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=190043#post190043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Shun the Smiling Lady, it quickly falls apart in the game setting as there's no reason why the Bronze Faction Exalted wouldn't frequently use that charm on the Anathema targeted by a Wyld Hunt. When you're on a Wyld Hunt, you want to cut the target off from his allies, and Shun the Smiling Lady is a wonderful charm for cutting off his closest and dearest friends. It will also cause a fair amount of confusion and worry in the target, as the love of his life suddenly rejects him - that coupled with the knowledge that he has transformed into one of the Anathema, would be a wonderful way of mentally breaking your target. &quot;I've just turned into a monster and my wife and children all dislike me now!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But StSL doesn't do...that. It doesn't make your friends and traveling companions abandon you or reject you (in all ways) or hate you. It makes you ugly, terminates romantic feelings towards you and prevents such feelings from being started. But it says nothing of feelings of friendship or loyalty - so the Solar's boyfriend might not feel romantic towards him anymore, that hardly means he rejects him and casts him out of his life and calls the cops on him. It creates a simple variable in the relationship, &quot;lack of romantic attachment,&quot; it doesn't inject a statement into the relationship that says &quot;you now despise your boyfriend, abandon him and sell him out!&quot; That's more of an ED charm, and these are very different things. At the least it terminates romantic feelings from the Solar's bf to the Solar, but the Solar's bf may have feelings of platonic affection or loyalty, and StSL does jack to those.<br /> <br /> If we're talking the 1e Charm, as was said, Appearance wasn't the biggest deal. Yes, in 2e, it affects your MDV when targeted by social attacks by pretty kitties, and being super ugly probably helps defenders of your social attacks resist them. I mean at least a little, StSL doesn't do much to hurt your social attacks if you're already built to throw 20 dice on an Excellency roll and have UMI, but for a Solar who is mostly about punching and relies more on unaugmented social rolls, it can be a pain.<br /> <br /> Really, &quot;romantic feelings&quot; and later &quot;romantic intimacies&quot; was terrible from a clarity standpoint of what the Charm will actually do to someone's social life, even if it's an evocative phrase.<br /> <br /> Also, wouldn't the Sidereals working with the Wyld Hunt have to know who you are to hit you with it? At least a little Just &quot;that guy we're chasing, whom we know exists but have never seen!&quot; shouldn't cut it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T06:14:45-07:00","id":190204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=188017#post188017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me see if I can come up with a few.<br /> <br /> Riding the Dragon: This transforms a person into a Lesser Elemental Dragon, and leaves them either an invalid for the rest of their short life, or permanently changes them into a Lesser Elemental Dragon. Yes, the Sidereal has to pay quite a bit for this to happen. It is still a very powerful effect. I'm not saying its a play balance issue, because the actual result doesn't seem that bad, but in character? That's some pretty serious mojo there.<br /> <br /> Avoidance Kata: Wow, I just lost that argument? You're really upset. Well, good thing I was never here to have this argument. I'm just walking in the room now. Let me sympathize with you. Or even better, let me lead you into this obvious deathtrap, which I can prove is NOT a deathtrap by gong first and showing you its safe. Oops, it was a deathtrap? Good thing I was never here.<br /> <br /> Neighbourhood Relocation Scheme: That's some pretty heavy mojo. I mean seriously heavy. I have no problem with the play balance, but that's like bringing a nuclear bomb to a sword fight.<br /> <br /> Many Missiles Bow Technique: Best healing charm in the game. One arrow heals five boxes of damage? Pretty awesome. Plus ending drought, making people fall in love, sowing fields of grain... That's a lot of stuff for one charm to do! Especially since it is scene-length. Again, I love this charm, but that's some pretty heavy magic. I mean, its bringing an orgy to a swordfight and ... winning?<br /> <br /> Efficient Secretary Technique: Who does research in libraries? Armies of grad students filing their findings so the Sidereal can have their secretary pull up facts as needed. Inventive use of this charm can do amazing things. Especially when you are trying to act like a secretive, all-knowing fate ninja.<br /> <br /> Avoiding the Truth Technique: Properly used, this is a convince anyone of anything Charm. It works so much better when you try to support your enemies than it does if you try to help yourself, of course.<br /> <br /> These are just a few of my favorite charms that I don't have issues with in terms of play balance, or play effect (so long as my PCs tell me they are buying them, so I can plan accordingly), but are just such heavy-handed effects.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry but I see some exaggeration here :<br /> <br /> Riding the Dragon: even if you sacrifice the dots (4xp in 2.5 IIRC) you don't get to &quot;keep&quot; he familiar/aquaintance. He becomes a real lesser elemental dragon and isn't your subordinate anymore, probably quite the opposite actually in the heavenly hierarchy. Though he may have/keep intimaces towards you. But don't forget that the tranformation itself is extremely painful (the target has to be restrained in order not to tear the prayer strip) and even if the recipient acquires divine immortality he may not feel in debt for your &quot;gift&quot;. Also the basic effect in itself suffers the same problems tan a lot of sumonns : fixed stats. It makes them powerful if you rush to get the charm early, but as your character progresses the impact is less and less important.<br /> <br /> Avoidance kata : it explicitly says that whatever effect the sid suffered remains. If you react before the deathtrap mortally wounds you good for you, but if you activate it too late, you'll be teleported but still die unless using other powers. Also if you activate it after &quot;losing&quot; to an opponent's argument you'll still be affected by the mental influence either natural or unnatural. Also it's limited to the first 2 actions after join battle/debate/war and creative storytellers may define other limitations for &quot;out of direct opposition&quot; situations like traps.<br /> <br /> Neighborhood Relocation Scheme : Like a lot of sidereal charms, extremely strong but narrow charms. It's up to you and your wits to put them into good use and adapt them to the situation, just like all the UMI that rolled against the target's essence instead of MDVs which is way easier, but way more narrow and limited than solar UMI.<br /> <br /> Many Missiles Bow Technique: rightfully nerfed. 1arrow and 1mote to heal many LHL , anybody can see the OPness.<br /> <br /> Efficient Secretary Technique : 2 motes for every question is quite a high tax, especially for sidereal mote pools. Believe me. It can be nice to fetch situationally crucial information like &quot;what's the name of this town's baker?&quot; so you can pose more convincingly as a local, but it can't find you anything really secret or &quot;lost&quot; on a large scale (IE only a few people still know the piece of information). So if your looking for a specific book quite &quot;popular&quot; in a frequently visited library it will work, but for rarely consulted books or books in an abandoned library, unless you stunt your way based on information you have (like &quot;which wing in the one dedicated to books about anathema's occult powers?&quot;) you hardly get anything out of the <br /> <br /> Avoiding the Truth Technique : actually it's a kind of specialized excellency plus it turns the social attack int an UMI costng 3wp to resist. I don't know solar UMI charms very well but i'm quite sure there should be something along those lines and less restrictive than having to work your way around the fact that your target(s) will be convinced you are lying.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now even if the &quot;narrowness&quot; of the charms is a tradeoff for their power it doesn't always mean the overall result is balanced. But except a few charms that make sense for sidereals (particularily pinalcle charms) or charms that are cornerstones designed to compensate for some of their huge weaknesses (avoidance kata, heartless maiden trance are perfect exemples) I don't think there is a sidereal charm that is blatantly on a higher power level than your typical solar charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T06:35:36-07:00","id":190218,"title":"","content":"Just as a note, StSM doesn't make you ugly anymore in 2.5, and the healing option in Many Missiles Bow also got a big nerfed (you roll your minimum damage, each success heal one HL instead of straight up healing [Archery] HLs like pre-Errata), though I still puzzle on the reason why they don't touch the Sid Medicine capstone and Wood Dragon Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-07-2014, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T07:46:50-07:00","id":190273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=190218#post190218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as a note, StSM doesn't make you ugly anymore in 2.5, and the healing option in Many Missiles Bow also got a big nerfed (you roll your minimum damage, each success heal one HL instead of straight up healing [Archery] HLs like pre-Errata), though I still puzzle on the reason why they don't touch the Sid Medicine capstone and Wood Dragon Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>2.5 Sids make up for this by being basically indestructible once they get their layered defenses up, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T10:48:31-07:00","id":190479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=190130#post190130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, &quot;romantic feelings&quot; and later &quot;romantic intimacies&quot; was terrible from a clarity standpoint of what the Charm will actually do to someone's social life, even if it's an evocative phrase.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I spent a lot of time reviewing the wording and hashing over readings as a result of this thread and I definitely hope that the 3e version talks over its implications a bit more. Even &quot;romantic&quot; is an incredibly loaded term.<br /> <br /> I've said in this thread that I have problems with Shun and mainly object to criticisms that seem hyperbolic and off-base, so putting my money where my mouth is, I think what I'd like to see done with Shun is something like this:<ul><li>As long as we have varying levels of Intimacies, make it easier to shake off its effects, but not automatic, if the Intimacy is Defining. Compromise between the &quot;love is a fickle amusement&quot; and &quot;love conquers all!&quot; camps. In particular, it should probably take less work for a strong intimacy to rebound if you just ding it and then immediately drop the commitment.</li> <li>While it's active, astrology (the mundane kind) and other kinds of fortunetelling can detect that the character is destined to never find love, <i>maybe</i> with a sufficiently boss roll they can detect that it was done on purpose.</li> <li>Sidereals have a lot of narrow hard counters and that's OK, but a long-term hard counter to a specific character niche is kind of a bad design space even when the character type is something very narrow. It needs to be calibrated such that it feels like an interesting challenge for a PC who relies heavily on their looks and sex appeal.</li> <li>Making it a Touch effect, as in 2.5, might be <i>too</i> extreme, but the idea that you have to actually be there to use it seems like a reasonable edit.</li> <li>Clarify the wording and implications.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-07-2014, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T12:50:51-07:00","id":190633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=190130#post190130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, wouldn't the Sidereals working with the Wyld Hunt have to know who you are to hit you with it? At least a little Just &quot;that guy we're chasing, whom we know exists but have never seen!&quot; shouldn't cut it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Logically Yurgen Kaneko, Samea and the rest of the Bull's circle, Raksi, Ma-ha-suchi, every famous Lunar or Solar Anathema out there, is going to be getting popped by this charm. The only way around it is to avoid doing anything important or game changing in Creation. <br /> <br /> Of course that's <i>exactly</i> the sort of things PCs are going to be doing and, again, logically they'll be getting popped by this charm by the Sidereal Exalted. <br /> <br /> As was mentioned, it was designed for PCs, and wasn't designed with the idea in mind that the NPCs were going to be using it against the PCs. That sometimes happens - something that looks like it would be cool in the PC's toolbox ends up being game-ruining in the NPC's toolbox. I mean, look at pre-nerf Maiden and Gambler stance - scene long perfect defense might be cool for PC's to use. It's much less cool when the Big Bad Evil Guy uses that scene long perfect defense and one of the players gets to to just stand there for the rest of the combat scene.<br /> <br /> Ultimately Shun the Smiling Lady was a cool idea, but it was implemented pretty poorly.<br /> <br /> ... now that I think about it though, maybe this explains Ma-ha-suchi's problems. He's just mad nobody will fall in love with him, and he thinks it's because he's been turned into a hideous monstrosity, so he's lashing out at the world. In fact however, it's because every morning after he goes pee, Chejop pops Ma-ha-suchi with Shun the Smiling Lady. Over the last 1200 years it's just become part of his daily routine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T13:02:55-07:00","id":190644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=190633#post190633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Logically Yurgen Kaneko, Samea and the rest of the Bull's circle, Raksi, Ma-ha-suchi, every famous Lunar or Solar Anathema out there, is going to be getting popped by this charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that's why so many signature characters have historically had the emotional intelligence of angsty teens, been virtually sociopathic in only forming positive intimacies to things and ideas, and also just being bitchy assholes in general in their behavior and social interactions. I think you're onto something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T14:07:20-07:00","id":190698,"title":"","content":"I don't see much value defending the first version of StSL. There are definitely positive and functional ways you can use it, and interesting, hard choices ways you may have to use it, but seems to be essentially what makes people who hate Sidereals pull out every time to explain why they hate Sidereals (and apparently almost nothing else in the Charmset).<br /> <br /> And it isn't what we have or will have in future, for good reasons (ask the Errata Team) - I guess, mainly because to avoid extremely alienating some of the audience and cause friction in games that takes on an adversarial dimension, not some bullshit where it is mathematically probable you are being messed with by it.<br /> <br /> Social network identity sabotage isn't particularly like StSL - it may be as inspiration fodder for a future Charm in the same genre though (&quot;Revenge Porn : The Charm&quot; probably not a good move though, if I think about it carefully).<br /> <br /> I will say again, for all that the Charm is flawed, the mindset, where significant fractions of the Sidereals, and humanity, are both dishonorable and ruthless enough to use that Charm out of spite on anyone who they regard as a significant threat or obstacle, let alone anyone they merely dislike.... that goes beyond any kind of realism or skepticism into pitch black cynicism (Jon Chung himself at least only suggested that the Sidereals would only do this because they, really, really believed in the Great Prophecy and at the end of the day, it is nicer than a Wyld Hunt. Which is still wrong, but not as crazily cynical.).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=189887#post189887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals that would use their powers in ways that the Fates don't want them to basically <i>don't exist</i> because they can opt to just <i>not choose those people</i>, having foreknowledge of how things will pan out.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, Rakan Thulio is a guy who exists. The Maidens, judging by their chosen, are a lot about getting what they get and understanding and managing the weave and order of events well enough to make sure it is what they want (more than just defining what they want or think ought to be and asserting it, or being so damn good the world has to bend its knee, or just inspiring their way to victory). Still fallible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T15:28:30-07:00","id":190802,"title":"","content":"Meh. All the conversation focusing on StSL is a little disappointing. That said, the issues I tended to have with the Charm were far far far more system skeleton related and less the specific Charm. Namely of course 1st edition's lack of social system and 2nd editions poor system skeleton and charm transition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 07-08-2014, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T18:00:28-07:00","id":190977,"title":"","content":"I am tired of every thread about Sidereal charms degenerating into denouncing/defending the existence of Shun the Smiling Lady, I would be happy to see it gone if it meant that this shit would stop.<br /> <br /> I think you could probably fold powerful curses into an application of Astrology and Craft Fate, a sort of fate artifact that goes way beyond the scope of a normal blessing or curse that requires extensive knowledge of the victim and access to objects that have been part of their destiny.<br /> It gives me this beautiful image of Rakan Thulio, aware that the Usurpation must come to pass working upon The Curse of Blades to give his lover the best gift he can under the circumstances... a death worthy of a true master of the sword.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T09:30:34-07:00","id":191470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=190698#post190698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On the other hand, Rakan Thulio is a guy who exists.</div> </div> </div> </div> This assumes the Maidens don't want a guy like Thulio to exist. I do mostly agree with the rest though; still, being the literal force that chooses sidereals would presumably let them choose who becomes a sidereal, and seeing their entire strand of fate would presumably let them make an informed decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T11:30:11-07:00","id":191552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=190977#post190977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am tired of every thread about Sidereal charms degenerating into denouncing/defending the existence of Shun the Smiling Lady, I would be happy to see it gone if it meant that this shit would stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen to that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T11:56:31-07:00","id":191585,"title":"","content":"New Charm: Shun Shun the Smiling Lady! When invoked, this charm immediately cancels all desire to discuss the Sidereal charm StSL. Debate continues as though the charm were never brought up. Charm designers are feverishly working on a Lunar variant, but with no success in sight...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T14:51:31-07:00","id":191708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/187960-sidereal-s-charms-strong-charms-myth-or-meme?p=190204#post190204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Riding the Dragon: even if you sacrifice the dots (4xp in 2.5 IIRC) you don't get to &quot;keep&quot; he familiar/aquaintance. He becomes a real lesser elemental dragon and isn't your subordinate anymore, probably quite the opposite actually in the heavenly hierarchy. Though he may have/keep intimaces towards you. But don't forget that the tranformation itself is extremely painful (the target has to be restrained in order not to tear the prayer strip) and even if the recipient acquires divine immortality he may not feel in debt for your &quot;gift&quot;. Also the basic effect in itself suffers the same problems tan a lot of sumonns : fixed stats. It makes them powerful if you rush to get the charm early, but as your character progresses the impact is less and less important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the part that I see as tricksy-ly OP is if you can use various other charms/RP to make someone a temporary acquaintance or familiar. Then just hold them for five actions &amp; you can shred their mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T19:05:19-07:00","id":191887,"title":"","content":"I use Shun the Smiling Lady to get away from Scourges; it should be able to remove the Intimacy of Sincere Love created through Tragic Love Amusement.<br /> <br /> But, yeah... Sidereals are missing <i>a lot</i> of basics. Still, TN reducers make me happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}